== Festivals ==
* Monthly
** Monthly festival (18th of each month)
* January
** New Year service (January 1)
** New Year grand prayer (January 1–7)
* February
** National Foundation Day service (February 11)
** Great Exorcism Festival (February 17–19)
* April
** Annual festival (April 8)
* June
** Great Purification (June 30)
* July
** Lantern festival (July 25–27)
** Children’s lantern float offering (July 25)
** Great festival of purification (July 26)
** Great festival of the people’s association (July 26)
** Lantern dedication safety prayer (July 27)
* October–November
** Shichi‑Go‑San prayers (October, November)
* November
** Harvest festival (November 23)
* December
** Emperor’s birthday festival (December 23)
** Year-end purification and New Year’s Eve festival (December 31)

== Sites of interest ==
* Exorcism drum bridge: Wooden bridge over the Tamura River<ref>{{Cite book|title=Aino Tsuchiyama History Guidebook|date=2015|publisher=Aino Tsuchiyama Fuchamoto Guide Association|page=9}}</ref>
* Arrow bamboo
* Kaido Bridge – from 1775 (An’ei 4) to 1939 (Shōwa 14), the Tōkaidō crossed the Tamura River on a floating board bridge at the shrine; depicted in Hiroshige’s “Spring Rain” of the series “The Fifty-three Stations of the Tōkaidō”. Rebuilt in July 2005 (Heisei 17) and named Kaido Bridge.

