* December
** Emperor’s birthday festival (December 23)
** Year-end purification and New Year’s Eve festival (December 31)

== Sites of interest ==
* Exorcism drum bridge: Wooden bridge over the Tamura River<ref>{{Cite book|title=Aino Tsuchiyama History Guidebook|date=2015|publisher=Aino Tsuchiyama Fuchamoto Guide Association|page=9}}</ref>
* Arrow bamboo
* Kaido Bridge – from 1775 (An’ei 4) to 1939 (Shōwa 14), the Tōkaidō crossed the Tamura River on a floating board bridge at the shrine; depicted in Hiroshige’s “Spring Rain” of the series “The Fifty-three Stations of the Tōkaidō”. Rebuilt in July 2005 (Heisei 17) and named Kaido Bridge.

